# Waivers for the vulnerability gate (scripts/gate.sh), in Trivy's .trivyignore
# format, so `trivy --ignorefile .trivyignore` reads the same file.
#
# One finding ID per line, followed by an expiry date. The gate rejects entries
# without one, and an entry stops applying after its date, so every waiver comes
# back for review. Write the reason, the owner and a ticket in the comment above
# the entry. Secrets can be waived by their Trivy rule ID the same way.
#
# Example:
#   # libfoo heap overflow, only reachable through a parser the app never calls.
#   # No Debian fix yet. Owner: alex. Ticket: #12.
#   CVE-2026-12345 exp:2026-12-31
